WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.620
All the boys were eager to ride Hurry.

2
00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:20.104
The ostrich traveled unbelievably quickly from Rockburg to Falconhurst.

3
00:00:20.105 --> 00:00:23.921
His speed led the boys to quarrel over who should own him.

4
00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:26.931
So I had to step in and end the arguing.

5
00:00:26.932 --> 00:00:29.324
"Hurry belongs to Jack," I said.

6
00:00:29.325 --> 00:00:34.188
"Jack weighs less than Fritz or Ernest, so he is more suited to ride the bird.

7
00:00:34.189 --> 00:00:38.300
And Franz is not yet strong enough to manage such a fast animal."

8
00:00:38.301 --> 00:00:41.655
Fritz started to protest. "But Father—"

9
00:00:41.656 --> 00:00:46.746
"And," I continued. "Jack was the one who captured him and named him.

10
00:00:46.747 --> 00:00:50.036
But you may all practice riding him occasionally.

11
00:00:50.037 --> 00:00:52.845
And anyone may ride him in an emergency."

12
00:00:52.846 --> 00:00:57.575
"Thank you, Father," said Jack. "But you must make me some goggles.

13
00:00:57.576 --> 00:01:02.910
Sometimes Hurry goes so fast that I have to shut my eyes to protect them from the wind."

14
00:01:02.911 --> 00:01:06.644
"Really?" I said. "I must do no such thing."

15
00:01:06.645 --> 00:01:09.844
"Why not?" Jack looked at me with amazement.

16
00:01:09.845 --> 00:01:13.652
"First because you cannot tell me I 'must' do anything.

17
00:01:13.653 --> 00:01:18.225
And second because you are perfectly capable of making goggles yourself."

18
00:01:18.226 --> 00:01:22.090
"I guess I do need an indoor activity," said Jack.

19
00:01:22.091 --> 00:01:25.418
Indeed our outdoor activities were coming to an end.

20
00:01:25.419 --> 00:01:30.464
Great black clouds and violent storms marked the beginning of another rainy season.

21
00:01:30.465 --> 00:01:35.306
Rockburg was a more spacious and pleasant place to spend the winter than Falconhurst.

22
00:01:35.307 --> 00:01:39.589
And we had many activities to keep us busy.

23
00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.392
Still the time dragged for all of us.

24
00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:45.507
"Let's build a kayak," said Fritz one day.

25
00:01:45.508 --> 00:01:50.214
"I've often longed for a more manageable boat than the canoe or the sailboat."

26
00:01:50.215 --> 00:01:52.578
"Oh yes, Father!" pleaded Ernest.

27
00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:55.872
"I've read about the kayaks that people build in Greenland."

28
00:01:55.873 --> 00:01:59.613
All the boys were immediately enthusiastic about the idea.

29
00:01:59.614 --> 00:02:01.579
But my wife was not.

30
00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:07.326
"'Your chances of drowning are already great enough with the canoe and the sailboat," she declared.

31
00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:11.090
"This is going to be a very safe boat," I reassured her.

32
00:02:11.091 --> 00:02:15.117
We started our boat-building by constructing a frame of whalebone.

33
00:02:15.118 --> 00:02:19.049
Then we used bamboo to strengthen the sides and build the deck.

34
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:24.329
That covered the whole length of the boat, leaving only a small square hole to sit in.

35
00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.742
We were totally caught up in our work.

36
00:02:26.743 --> 00:02:30.769
By the time the kayak was complete, the rainy season was over.

37
00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:34.510
The kayak was just narrow enough to fit through our front door.

38
00:02:34.511 --> 00:02:37.933
We completed its construction in the open air.

39
00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:41.860
"That's a funny-looking boat," said little Franz.

40
00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.069
"Do you really think it will float?"

41
00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:49.122
"Look," said Fritz. "It's so light that I can pick it up with one hand."

42
00:02:49.123 --> 00:02:53.533
"It still seems awfully fragile to me," said my wife.

43
00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:59.011
Before she would allow him to try the kayak, she insisted on making him a special swimsuit.

44
00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:04.306
"I don't want him to drown if his boat is punctured by a sharp rock," she explained.

45
00:03:04.307 --> 00:03:09.553
"The kayak won't break like a soap bubble," I said with some exasperation.

46
00:03:09.554 --> 00:03:12.253
But I agreed to help her make the swimsuit.

47
00:03:12.254 --> 00:03:16.724
My wife said that Fritz needed a jacket, pants, and cap.

48
00:03:16.725 --> 00:03:21.292
We made these garments from linen and then lined them with another piece of fabric.

49
00:03:21.293 --> 00:03:24.048
Everything was then coated with rubber.

50
00:03:24.049 --> 00:03:30.634
We left a small hole, so that the garments could be inflated by blowing air between the linen and the lining.

51
00:03:30.635 --> 00:03:34.738
At last it was time for Fritz to take the kayak on a test voyage.

52
00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:36.930
We all gathered on the beach.

53
00:03:36.931 --> 00:03:41.288
I got out the canoe so my wife could see we were ready to rescue him if needed.

54
00:03:41.289 --> 00:03:45.215
Fritz stepped into the kayak and began to inflate his swimsuit.

55
00:03:45.216 --> 00:03:48.609
Fritz soon puffed up so that we could hardly recognize him.

56
00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:54.010
The boys shouted with laughter. Even my wife could not resist a smile.

57
00:03:54.011 --> 00:03:57.627
"You look so funny!" cried little Franz.

58
00:03:57.628 --> 00:04:01.548
The kayak floated lightly on the bay as Fritz began to paddle.

59
00:04:01.549 --> 00:04:04.022
First he darted straight ahead.

60
00:04:04.023 --> 00:04:07.327
Then he turned to the left and circled to the right.

61
00:04:07.328 --> 00:04:11.790
Finally he flipped on his side while his mother uttered a shriek of terror.

62
00:04:11.791 --> 00:04:14.458
"Oh no!" she cried.

63
00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:16.841
But Fritz quickly righted himself.

64
00:04:16.842 --> 00:04:20.448
"All is well!" he shouted to us over the water.

65
00:04:20.449 --> 00:04:24.012
"It may be just a tiny boat," I said to my wife.

66
00:04:24.013 --> 00:04:26.929
"But it's a sturdy one, and it won't sink."

67
00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:30.804
"Hooray for Fritz and the kayak!" yelled Jack.

68
00:04:30.805 --> 00:04:33.760
The other boys shouted their approval too.

69
00:04:33.761 --> 00:04:37.849
Fritz raised his arm in salute and turned the kayak away from shore.

70
00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:42.947
We watched him for a few minutes, and then suddenly I realized something dreadful.

71
00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:45.523
The tide was carrying him out to sea!

72
00:04:45.524 --> 00:04:47.890
"Ernest! Jack!" I said.

73
00:04:47.891 --> 00:04:51.316
"Help me launch the canoe. We must rescue your brother."

74
00:04:51.317 --> 00:04:53.244
We pushed off from shore.

75
00:04:53.245 --> 00:05:03.500
My wife wrapped her arms around little Franz and said, "I knew an accident would happen in that horrid soap bubble."
